# =============================================================================
# backend/.dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/Dockerfile's build context is THIS directory (docker-compose.yml
# uses `build: ./backend`, not the project root), so this file -- not the
# root .dockerignore -- is what keeps local dev cruft out of `COPY . /app/`.
# Without it, anything a developer happens to have on disk locally
# (__pycache__/, a stray .venv/, editor state) would get copied into the
# image and bloat it, and in __pycache__'s case could even ship .pyc files
# built against a different Python version than the image's.
# =============================================================================

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

*.log
